{#
   SHAPE 1 — the list page. S59's proposed deliverable, in prototype form.

   Search and filters ALWAYS VISIBLE, applied filters as removable chips, a
   count that is a sentence, a CSV control, and an empty state that offers the
   widening action instead of saying nothing.

   Slots:

     title        page heading
     action       {label, url} — the page's one primary action, top right
     filters      raw form controls, supplied by the caller via the `filters`
                  block (this is an *embed*, not an include, for that reason)
     chips        list of {label, url} — url REMOVES that filter
     count        the sentence: "11 machines · 3 catégories"
     widen        {label, url} — shown in the empty state, e.g. "voir toutes
                  les dates". This is the difference between a dead end and a
                  way out.
     csv_url      renders the download control. ⚠️ OMIT IT UNLESS IT WORKS.
                  S54 deleted a fake Export button whose JS was three alert()
                  stubs; re-adding a decorative one would undo that session.

   ⚠️ A CSV of anything user-shaped is personal data leaving the building. It
   must sit behind the same access_control line as the page, and it must never
   carry badge UIDs — that is S38's live finding.
#}
{% set _chips = chips|default([]) %}

<div class="pp-list-head">
    <h1>{{ title|default('') }}</h1>
    {% if action|default(null) %}
        <a class="pp-btn" href="{{ action.url }}">{{ action.label }}</a>
    {% endif %}
</div>

<form class="pp-filters" method="get" action="">
    {% block filters %}{% endblock %}
    <div class="pp-field">
        <label for="pp-submit-spacer" class="visually-hidden" aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;</label>
        <button id="pp-submit-spacer" class="pp-btn" type="submit">Filtrer</button>
    </div>
</form>

{% if _chips is not empty %}
    <div class="pp-chips">
        {% for chip in _chips %}
            <span class="pp-chip">
                {{ chip.label }}
                <a href="{{ chip.url }}" aria-label="Retirer le filtre {{ chip.label }}">✕</a>
            </span>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endif %}

<div class="pp-count">
    <span>{{ count|default('') }}</span>
    {% if csv_url|default('') %}
        <a href="{{ csv_url }}" download>⬇ Télécharger en CSV</a>
    {% endif %}
</div>

{% block results %}{% endblock %}
